  "notes": {
    "question": "would a per-month description fingerprint have caught the Austin storage break in 2026-07, and would it have fired on anything else in the window?",
    "policy": "MEASUREMENT ONLY. Nothing here is wired into ingestion. No value below is derived from a single description: shapes are hashes discarded after grouping, tokens are discarded after counting, and only counts and percentages are written.",
    "normalisation": "lowercase; every run of digits to '#'; whitespace collapsed to one space",
    "shape": "sha1 of the normalised description, first 10 hex — grouping only, never written",
    "token": "lowercased runs of three or more letters — counted only, never written",
    "marginalRequestCost": "none. `description` is already in the ingest's $select because Austin's classifier needs it, and the window is already re-read in full every ingest (RECOUNT_MONTHS=13).",
    "v2Reconstruction": "v2_solar = today's solar classification UNION every row whose work_class is 'Auxiliary Power' — the one mapping line Round 50 removed. A set union over the current classifier, not a second copy of the old one.",
    "sanAntonioReach": "not measurable. San Antonio's export has no description column — measured in docs/audits/round-51-storage.json (sanAntonio.columns / sanAntonio.headers) and cited rather than re-fetched. Every San Antonio category is classified by the city's own permit type, so there is no description vocabulary there to fingerprint.",
    "where": "issue_date between '2025-09-01T00:00:00' and '2026-10-15T22:14:28' AND (permit_type_desc in ('Electrical Permit', 'Plumbing Permit', 'Mechanical Permit') OR work_class in ('Auxiliary Power', 'Roof') OR upper(work_class) like '%ROOF%' OR upper(permit_type_desc) like '%ROOF%' OR upper(description) like '%ROOF%' OR upper(description) like '%SOLAR%' OR upper(description) like '%PHOTOVOLTAIC%')"
  },
